-- The minimal seed: two unary predicates, one rule, one query.
--
-- `isHuman` is an INPUT predicate (a stored record field, so no clauses);
-- `is mortal` is a COMPUTED one with a single clause. Everything the relational
-- lowering does to a real module — selection, ANF, the signed dependency graph,
-- stratification, query capture — is present here at the smallest size that
-- still has all of it, which makes this the fixture to read first when a golden
-- moves.
--
-- Each directive below carries its L4-oracle value on the line after it, as a
-- `-- L4 oracle ==>` comment produced by `l4 run mortality.l4` — the
-- differential harness's expectation, kept outside the emitted program per
-- BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R11 and kept in exactly one place per directive.

DECLARE Person HAS
    isHuman IS A BOOLEAN

@export
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is mortal` IF p's isHuman

#EVAL `is mortal` (Person WITH isHuman IS TRUE)
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

#EVAL `is mortal` (Person WITH isHuman IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE
